<title>UK: SOCCER-FRANK CLARK FACTFILE.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-FRANK CLARK FACTFILE.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is factfile on Frank</p>
<p>Clark who has resigned as manager of English premier league</p>
<p>bottom club Nottingham Forest:</p>
<p>1943: Born Durham, September 9.</p>
<p>1961: Won F.A. Amateur Cup medal with Crook Town.</p>
<p>1962: Joined Newcastle, where went on to make 388 league</p>
<p>appearances.</p>
<p>1965: Won second division championship medal.</p>
<p>1969: Won UEFA Cup winner's medal.</p>
<p>1975: Joined Nottingham Forest on a free transfer, where</p>
<p>made 116 appearances.</p>
<p>1978: Won league championship medal and League Cup winner's</p>
<p>medal.</p>
<p>1979: Won European Cup and League Cup winners' medals</p>
<p>1983: Became manager of Leyton Orient.</p>
<p>1991: Became managing director at Orient.</p>
<p>1993: Became manager of Nottingham Forest.</p>
<p>1996: Resigned as manager of Nottingham Forest.</p>
</text>
